# SpecGate CODEOWNERS
#
# run.md §16 and ADR-013 (§13.3) require that changes to the design, schemas,
# and tamper-sensitive paths get an explicit review. This file is the
# repo-level backstop; the `tamper` gate (M5.C) is the agent-session backstop.
#
# Replace the @owner placeholder below with the real owner handle(s) when the
# project moves out of pre-development.

# Design + plan — the sources of truth for every change.
/run.md                           @owner
/PLAN.md                          @owner

# Schemas: the source-of-truth zod definitions and generated JSON Schema.
/packages/core/src/schemas/       @owner
/schemas/                         @owner

# Tamper-sensitive runtime config paths (users' repos — mirrored here for
# dogfooding from M3 onward).
/.specgate/                       @owner

# CI/CD — avoid unreviewed changes to the non-bypassable backstop (run.md §9.5).
/.github/workflows/               @owner
/.github/CODEOWNERS               @owner
